// One row per card: [angle, top, bottom]. Read by the shared gradient rule in the
// style block as --grad-angle/--grad-top/--grad-bottom, and applied inline to each
// section. Living here rather than as per-card CSS rules means every card in the
// page is visible in one place and the guard below can check all of them.
//
// Keyed by the card's own ident (project `key` or skill-group `ident`), so a colour
// travels with the card it belongs to rather than with a source position that a
// reorder would break. `to top` puts the first colour at the top of the card; the
// portfolio cards use staggered diagonals so neighbours do not read as a pair.
// [angle, top, mid, bottom] -- three stops, so every card has a colour at each end
// and a hue shift through the middle. The pairs are complementary rather than
// tonal: Professional Skills already runs orange into purple, and the same
// warm-cool opposition is now scattered across the skill groups and portfolio
// cards so it reads as a system instead of a one-off. `warm` is the low-hue end
// (rust, amber, teal leaning warm), `cool` the high-hue end (violet, indigo,
// blue), with the mid stop sitting between them so the transition is a real
// gradient rather than a hard two-tone split.
